Start here to add push notifications to a mobile app and connect it to the correct sending backend. Choose the delivery method already approved for the application: **FCM**, **direct APNs**, or an **AWS SNS-backed integration**. FCM mobile setup, direct APNs setup, and backend publishing have separate procedures.

**Outcome:** choose a matching mobile/provider/backend path, identify its prerequisites, and follow the setup pages in order. Notification-tap routing uses the application’s approved deep-link and authentication contracts.

> **Confidential — Enterprise internal use only.** Keep device tokens, endpoint/subscription identifiers, user mappings, provider credentials, and internal package access protected. Never put credentials or customer/order payloads in notification bodies, logs, screenshots, or AI prompts.

## 1. Understand the delivery flow

| Component | Responsibility |
| :--- | :--- |
| Mobile application | Registers with its notification provider, obtains the current token, and handles received notifications according to platform/app state. |
| Application backend | Associates the token/endpoint with the authorized user and application, applies notification preferences, and requests delivery. |
| AWS SNS | Maintains platform endpoints, supports direct publishing and topic subscriptions, and forwards messages to the configured provider. |
| FCM | Cross-platform messaging service; Apple delivery still uses APNs underneath. Its registration token is distinct from an APNs token. |
| APNs | Apple push provider, used directly by the APNs path or underneath FCM on Apple devices. |
| Device OS/application | Determines presentation and handling according to permissions, payload type, app state, and platform constraints. |

Match the sender to the chosen token/provider path. Direct APNs and FCM-on-iOS are separate integrations; do not submit their tokens interchangeably or initialize duplicate notification handlers for the same path. [SNS mobile endpoints](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sns/latest/dg/mobile-platform-endpoint.html), [FCM overview](https://firebase.google.com/docs/cloud-messaging).

<MermaidZoom title="Registration creates a target; publishing requests delivery">

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant APP as Mobile App
    participant PROVIDER as FCM or APNs
    participant API as Application Backend
    participant SNS as AWS SNS
    participant DB as Backend Storage
    APP->>PROVIDER: Register through the configured mobile integration
    PROVIDER-->>APP: Current provider token
    APP->>API: Supply token through the approved authenticated contract
    API->>SNS: Create or reconcile endpoint under the platform application
    SNS-->>API: Endpoint ARN
    API->>DB: Store authorized user, app and endpoint association
