  order: 3
---

import { Tabs, TabItem } from '@astrojs/starlight/components';
import MermaidZoom from '../components/mermaid-zoom.astro';

Use this page for **FCM on Android and FCM on iOS through APNs**, including React Native. Direct APNs uses a separate setup page. Read [Notification Guidelines](./notification-guidelines.mdx) first.

**Outcome:** register the current FCM token, process messages, and handle an open event through the application's authorized startup flow.

> **Confidential — Enterprise internal use only.** Use approved non-production Firebase projects/devices for initial verification. Never put Firebase Admin/service-account keys, APNs private keys, backend credentials, tokens, or customer/order payloads in mobile source, screenshots, logs, or AI prompts.

## 1. Choose the implementation and prepare the bindings

The two helper files are reusable templates, **not a replacement for native configuration or the host application's backend and navigation**. Replace their package names, resources, and required bindings before compiling.

| Helper | Responsibility |
| :--- | :--- |
| `FcmService` | Messaging callbacks, current token/refresh, and handoff to the app's registration/refresh worker. |
| `NotificationService` | Presentation permission, native presentation policy, notification-open capture, and deferred consumption after app readiness. |

The baseline uses ordinary notification/notification-plus-data messages, generic “open updates” behavior, and no payload-supplied URLs. Android uses the documented HTTP v1/`onMessageReceived` callback path; newer AndroidConfigV2 callbacks require the matching SDK/server integration. Do not mix that migration into this template without validating the actual versions. [Firebase message reception](https://firebase.google.com/docs/cloud-messaging/android/receive-messages), [Android callback migration](https://firebase.google.com/docs/cloud-messaging/send/v2-api).

### Required application bindings

| Binding | Host application supplies |
| :--- | :--- |
| Token synchronization | Durable enqueue and authenticated backend registration/update using the **current account at execution**; report actual success/failure. |
| Content refresh | Bounded/background-safe enqueue to reload authorized current data. Receiving a push must never place an order or mark one successful. |
| Open action | A synchronous acceptance function returning `true` only when startup, authentication, navigation, and current-user access are ready. |
| Account change/opt-out | Server association/subscription cleanup and cancellation/reconciliation of pending work according to the real API. |
| Safe diagnostics | Fixed error categories without token, payload, raw provider errors, or personal data. |

These are **template callbacks**, not additional Enterprise SDK APIs. Callbacks used synchronously must be non-throwing and fast; use a durable worker for network work and report enqueue failures safely. No registration endpoint, deep-link scheme, order ID schema, or logout API is invented here. A backend outage must not be treated as successful registration.

## 2. Register the application in Firebase

