Use this page when the application's **Java backend sends notifications through AWS SNS**. Mobile registration uses [FCM Mobile Setup](./fcm-mobile-setup.mdx) or [Direct APNs Setup](./apns-ios-setup.mdx).

**Outcome:** implement a configured SNS adapter with explicit endpoint, subscription, and publish outcomes, then connect it to the application's authenticated API and storage.

> **Confidential — Enterprise internal use only.** Keep AWS/provider credentials in the approved backend bindings. Do not log device tokens, user/email mappings, payloads, private ARNs, or raw SDK exceptions. No live registration, subscription, or send is required simply to copy this template.

## 1. Confirm the supported SDK and configuration

**Compatibility:** older integrations use `com.amazonaws:aws-java-sdk-sns` and `AmazonSNSClient`. AWS SDK for Java **1.x reached end of support on December 31, 2025**. The new template below uses **2.x** (`software.amazon.awssdk`) and Java 17-compatible source. Do not paste it into a 1.x client or silently upgrade an existing backend without its compatibility review. [AWS Java migration guidance](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sdk-for-java/latest/developer-guide/migration.html), [1.x support status](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sdk-for-java/latest/developer-guide/migration-find-apps-using-v1.html).

Ask the backend/platform owner for:

| Configuration | Meaning |
| :--- | :--- |
| AWS Region and workload identity | Approved account/Region and runtime role/credential binding. The sample Region is not an Enterprise-wide default. |
| `MOBILE_PUSH_NOTIFICATION_FCM_PLATFORM_APP_ARN` | Existing SNS platform application for FCM tokens. SNS commonly labels this provider `GCM`. |
| `MOBILE_PUSH_NOTIFICATION_APNS_PLATFORM_APP_ARN` | Existing direct APNs platform application, matching the Apple environment. |
| Approved SNS Topic ARNs | Separate resources for authorized audiences. Do not reuse either platform-application variable as a topic. |
| Authenticated registration/send contracts | Actual user/device ownership, input validation, preferences, and permission to send. |
| Durable persistence/operation coordination | Endpoint associations, subscriptions, current-account checks, concurrency, and unknown-outcome reconciliation. |

SNS platform applications/provider credentials are owner-managed prerequisites. This adapter does not create them, request permissions, or define a new REST endpoint.

