## 3. Copy the configured client factory

**File: `SnsClientFactory.java`**

```java
package com.example.mychicken.push;

import java.time.Duration;
import software.amazon.awssdk.core.retry.RetryPolicy;
import software.amazon.awssdk.regions.Region;
import software.amazon.awssdk.services.sns.SnsClient;

public final class SnsClientFactory {
    private SnsClientFactory() {}

    public static SnsClient create(String region) {
        if (region == null || region.isBlank()) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("SNS Region is required");
        }
        return SnsClient.builder()
            .region(Region.of(region))
            // Default credential provider chain: bind the approved workload role.
            // No embedded access keys. No hidden SDK retries for uncertain writes.
            .overrideConfiguration(c -> c
                .retryPolicy(RetryPolicy.none())
                .apiCallTimeout(Duration.ofSeconds(30))
                .apiCallAttemptTimeout(Duration.ofSeconds(15)))
            .build();
    }
}
```

Create one shared client for the appropriate Region and inject it into the adapter; close it at application shutdown. In an existing Spring application, expose it through the established configuration/bean mechanism rather than field-injecting a cast `AmazonSNSClient`.

The template disables SDK retries to avoid hidden repeats of uncertain writes. It does not guarantee exactly-once delivery. The timeout values are illustrative and require operational approval; read-only recovery and any explicitly safe retries belong to the operation coordinator. Runtime credentials come from the approved provider chain/role, not strings in source. [AWS credential provider chain](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sdk-for-java/latest/developer-guide/credentials-chain.html).

## 4. Copy the payload builder

**File: `PushPayloads.java`**

```java
package com.example.mychicken.push;

import com.fasterxml.jackson.core.JsonProcessingException;
import com.fasterxml.jackson.databind.ObjectMapper;
import java.nio.charset.StandardCharsets;
import java.util.Map;

public final class PushPayloads {
    private static final String TITLE = "My Chicken App";
    private static final String BODY = "An update is available. Open the app to view it.";
    private final ObjectMapper json;

    public PushPayloads(ObjectMapper json) {
        this.json = java.util.Objects.requireNonNull(json);
    }

    // Generic synthetic alert only. Business-specific data requires a reviewed contract.
    public String genericUpdate() {
        String fcm = encode(Map.of("fcmV1Message", Map.of("message", Map.of(
            "notification", Map.of("title", TITLE, "body", BODY)
        ))));
        String apns = encode(Map.of("aps", Map.of(
            "alert", Map.of("title", TITLE, "body", BODY), "sound", "default"
        )));
        requireWithin(fcm, 4096);
        requireWithin(apns, 4096);
        // SNS requires each platform-specific JSON value to be a JSON-encoded string.
        // GCM is SNS's wire key for the FCM provider; it is not a request to use legacy FCM.
        String envelope = encode(Map.of(
            "default", BODY, "GCM", fcm, "APNS", apns, "APNS_SANDBOX", apns
        ));
        // Conservative template guard for this small alert, not a universal SNS limit.
        requireWithin(envelope, 8192);
        return envelope;
    }

    private String encode(Object value) {
        try {
            return json.writeValueAsString(value);
        } catch (JsonProcessingException failure) {
            throw new IllegalStateException("Push serialization failed");
        }
    }

    private static void requireWithin(String value, int bytes) {
        if (value.getBytes(StandardCharsets.UTF_8).length > bytes) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Push payload exceeds template size limit");
        }
    }
}
```

This builder intentionally sends only a generic synthetic update. It does not accept arbitrary order/customer data. Replace the public text through the approved content/localization design before production use.

The structure is:

```text
SNS MessageStructure = json
└── Message JSON
    ├── default: plain fallback text
    ├── GCM: JSON STRING containing fcmV1Message → message → notification
    ├── APNS: JSON STRING containing aps → alert/sound
    └── APNS_SANDBOX: JSON STRING containing aps → alert/sound
```

`aps` contains a separate alert object; it must not reference itself. SNS platform values are encoded **strings**, not nested objects in the outer SNS envelope. The `GCM` wire key can carry the supported FCM HTTP v1 structure. [SNS FCM v1 payload](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sns/latest/dg/sns-fcm-v1-payloads.html), [platform-specific JSON publishing](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sns/latest/api/API_Publish.html).

Size checks here cover this small template's serialized provider/envelope strings; they are not a complete validator for every provider option or topic policy. For routes such as FCM topics, apply the route-specific rules from [Notification Guidelines](./notification-guidelines.mdx).

## 5. Copy the SNS adapter

**File: `SnsPushService.java`**

```java
package com.example.mychicken.push;

import java.util.Map;
import java.util.Objects;
import java.util.Set;
import java.util.regex.Matcher;
import java.util.regex.Pattern;
import software.amazon.awssdk.core.exception.SdkClientException;
import software.amazon.awssdk.services.sns.SnsClient;
import software.amazon.awssdk.services.sns.model.*;

public final class SnsPushService {
    private static final Pattern PLATFORM = Pattern.compile(
        "^(arn:(?:aws|aws-us-gov|aws-cn):sns:[a-z0-9-]+:[0-9]{12}:)app/(GCM|APNS|APNS_SANDBOX)/([A-Za-z0-9_.-]+)$"
    );
    private final SnsClient sns;
    private final String platformApplicationArn;
    private final String endpointPrefix;
    private final Set<String> allowedTopics;
    private final PushPayloads payloads;

    // Construct one configured service per actual platform application/environment.
    public SnsPushService(
        SnsClient sns, String platformApplicationArn,
        Set<String> allowedTopics, PushPayloads payloads
    ) {
        this.sns = Objects.requireNonNull(sns);
        this.payloads = Objects.requireNonNull(payloads);
        Matcher match = PLATFORM.matcher(Objects.requireNonNull(platformApplicationArn));
        if (!match.matches()) throw new IllegalArgumentException("Invalid platform application ARN");
        this.platformApplicationArn = platformApplicationArn;
        this.endpointPrefix = match.group(1) + "endpoint/" + match.group(2) + "/" + match.group(3) + "/";
        this.allowedTopics = Set.copyOf(allowedTopics);
        for (String topic : this.allowedTopics) {
            if (!topic.startsWith(match.group(1)) ||
                !topic.substring(match.group(1).length()).matches("[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,256}")) {
                throw new IllegalArgumentException("Expected same-account/Region standard topic ARN");
            }
        }
    }

    public String registerCurrentToken(String currentToken, String storedEndpointArn) {
        requireText(currentToken, "Current provider token is required");
        String endpoint = storedEndpointArn;
        if (endpoint == null || endpoint.isBlank()) {
            // Persist the returned ARN BEFORE proceeding, through the host coordinator.
            // This method returns creation only; call verifyEndpoint after that commit.
            return createEndpoint(currentToken);
        }
        requireEndpoint(endpoint);
        // No automatic replacement creation on NotFound/conflict; owner reconciles it.
        verifyEndpoint(endpoint, currentToken);
        return endpoint;
    }

    private String createEndpoint(String token) {
        try {
            String arn = sns.createPlatformEndpoint(CreatePlatformEndpointRequest.builder()
                .platformApplicationArn(platformApplicationArn).token(token).build()).endpointArn();
            if (arn == null || !arn.startsWith(endpointPrefix) || arn.length() == endpointPrefix.length()) {
                throw new UnknownWriteOutcome("Endpoint creation response not verified; reconcile before retry");
            }
            return arn;
        } catch (SnsException failure) {
            if (failure.statusCode() >= 500) {
                throw new UnknownWriteOutcome("SNS write failed with uncertain outcome; reconcile before retry");
            }
            throw failure;
        } catch (SdkClientException failure) {
            throw new UnknownWriteOutcome("Endpoint creation outcome unknown; reconcile before retry");
        }
        // SNS service rejections propagate. Do not parse an exception message for an ARN.
    }

    public void verifyEndpoint(String endpointArn, String currentToken) {
        requireEndpoint(endpointArn);
        requireText(currentToken, "Current provider token is required");
        Map<String, String> attributes = sns.getEndpointAttributes(
            GetEndpointAttributesRequest.builder().endpointArn(endpointArn).build()).attributes();
        if (!currentToken.equals(attributes.get("Token")) ||
            !"true".equalsIgnoreCase(attributes.get("Enabled"))) {
            try {
                sns.setEndpointAttributes(SetEndpointAttributesRequest.builder()
                    .endpointArn(endpointArn)
                    .attributes(Map.of("Token", currentToken, "Enabled", "true")).build());
            } catch (SnsException failure) {
                if (failure.statusCode() >= 500) {
                    throw new UnknownWriteOutcome("SNS update outcome uncertain; reconcile before retry");
                }
                throw failure;
            } catch (SdkClientException failure) {
                throw new UnknownWriteOutcome("Endpoint update outcome unknown; reconcile before retry");
            }
            Map<String, String> updated = sns.getEndpointAttributes(
                GetEndpointAttributesRequest.builder().endpointArn(endpointArn).build()).attributes();
            if (!currentToken.equals(updated.get("Token")) ||
                !"true".equalsIgnoreCase(updated.get("Enabled"))) {
                throw new IllegalStateException("Endpoint state not verified");
            }
        }
    }

    public String subscribe(String topicArn, String endpointArn) {
        requireTopic(topicArn);
        requireEndpoint(endpointArn);
        try {
            String subscription = sns.subscribe(SubscribeRequest.builder()
                .topicArn(topicArn).protocol("application").endpoint(endpointArn)
                .returnSubscriptionArn(true).build()).subscriptionArn();
            if (subscription == null || allowedTopics.stream().noneMatch(topic ->
                subscription.startsWith(topic + ":") && subscription.length() > topic.length() + 1)) {
                throw new UnknownWriteOutcome("Subscription response not verified; reconcile before retry");
            }
            return subscription;
        } catch (SnsException failure) {
            if (failure.statusCode() >= 500) {
                throw new UnknownWriteOutcome("SNS write failed with uncertain outcome; reconcile before retry");
            }
            throw failure;
        } catch (SdkClientException failure) {
            throw new UnknownWriteOutcome("Subscription outcome unknown; reconcile before retry");
        }
    }

    public void unsubscribe(String storedSubscriptionArn) {
        requireSubscription(storedSubscriptionArn);
        try {
            sns.unsubscribe(UnsubscribeRequest.builder()
                .subscriptionArn(storedSubscriptionArn).build());
        } catch (SnsException failure) {
            if (failure.statusCode() >= 500) {
                throw new UnknownWriteOutcome("SNS write failed with uncertain outcome; reconcile before retry");
            }
            throw failure;
        } catch (SdkClientException failure) {
            throw new UnknownWriteOutcome("Unsubscription outcome unknown; reconcile before retry");
        }
    }

    public String publishToEndpoint(String authorizedEndpointArn) {
        requireEndpoint(authorizedEndpointArn);
        return publish(PublishRequest.builder().targetArn(authorizedEndpointArn)
            .messageStructure("json").message(payloads.genericUpdate()).build());
    }

    public String publishToTopic(String authorizedTopicArn) {
        requireTopic(authorizedTopicArn);
        return publish(PublishRequest.builder().topicArn(authorizedTopicArn)
            .messageStructure("json").message(payloads.genericUpdate()).build());
    }

    private String publish(PublishRequest request) {
        try {
            String id = sns.publish(request).messageId();
            if (id == null || id.isBlank()) {
                throw new UnknownWriteOutcome("Publish response has no message ID; reconcile before retry");
            }
            return id; // SNS acceptance only, not device receipt/display.
        } catch (SnsException failure) {
            if (failure.statusCode() >= 500) {
                throw new UnknownWriteOutcome("SNS write failed with uncertain outcome; reconcile before retry");
            }
            throw failure;
        } catch (SdkClientException failure) {
            throw new UnknownWriteOutcome("Publish outcome unknown; reconcile before retry");
        }
    }

    private void requireTopic(String arn) {
        if (!allowedTopics.contains(arn)) throw new IllegalArgumentException("Topic is not approved");
    }

    private void requireEndpoint(String arn) {
        if (arn == null || !arn.startsWith(endpointPrefix) || arn.length() == endpointPrefix.length()) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Endpoint does not match configured platform application");
        }
    }

    private void requireSubscription(String arn) {
        if (arn == null || allowedTopics.stream().noneMatch(topic ->
            arn.startsWith(topic + ":") && arn.length() > topic.length() + 1)) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Subscription does not match approved topics");
        }
    }

    private static void requireText(String value, String message) {
        if (value == null || value.isBlank()) throw new IllegalArgumentException(message);
    }

    public static final class UnknownWriteOutcome extends RuntimeException {
        public UnknownWriteOutcome(String safeMessage) { super(safeMessage); }
    }
}
```

### Construct one adapter per configured platform application

Use the approved Region, platform-application ARN, and set of authorized **standard SNS topic** ARNs:

```java
// Composition fragment; configuration values come from the approved environment.
SnsClient sns = SnsClientFactory.create(approvedRegion);
PushPayloads payloads = new PushPayloads(existingConfiguredObjectMapper);
SnsPushService push = new SnsPushService(
    sns, approvedPlatformApplicationArn, approvedTopicArns, payloads
);
```

`approvedRegion`, `existingConfiguredObjectMapper`, `approvedPlatformApplicationArn`, and `approvedTopicArns` are **host-provided values**, not library exports. This adapter intentionally limits topics to the same Region/account and standard topic names. Expand cross-account/FIFO behavior only with a reviewed contract.

ARN validation prevents obvious resource-type/provider mix-ups; it does **not** authorize a user. Before calling the adapter, the application must resolve the endpoint/subscription from its protected current-user records and confirm recipient/topic entitlement. Do not accept an arbitrary caller-supplied ARN as authorization.

## 6. Register, persist, and verify in separate steps

The host registration coordinator must serialize work for the application/installation/account association and reconcile stale or overlapping requests.

1. Authenticate the registration request and validate the current installation/account/provider mapping.
2. Obtain the current provider token and read the stored endpoint association from the real database.
3. Call `registerCurrentToken(currentToken, storedEndpointArn)` with that stored association.
4. If no endpoint was stored, the method returns the created/existing SNS ARN **without claiming readiness**. Persist the returned association durably before further mutations. If persistence fails, preserve the unresolved operation evidence and reconcile; do not create another endpoint blindly.
5. Call `verifyEndpoint(endpointArn, currentToken)` after the association is persisted. It reads SNS state and updates the current token/enabled flag only when necessary, then verifies the result.
6. Report registration complete only after the correct association is stored and endpoint readiness is verified. A returned creation ARN alone is insufficient.

For a stored endpoint, `registerCurrentToken` already verifies it; a final read-only verification can still be used by the coordinator. Invalid/missing/deleted endpoint errors are not silently converted into another creation. Resolve those outcomes against stored operation evidence and current SNS state before deciding the next authorized action. [AWS endpoint lifecycle](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sns/latest/dg/mobile-platform-endpoint.html).

The API can return an existing matching endpoint or reject a token/settings conflict. Do not extract an ARN by regular-expression parsing of the exception message and then assume ownership. [CreatePlatformEndpoint contract](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sns/latest/api/API_CreatePlatformEndpoint.html).

