## 7. Subscribe, publish, and unsubscribe

| Operation | Call | Required host behavior |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Subscribe | `subscribe(topicArn, endpointArn)` | Validate audience/current preferences, coordinate the operation, and persist the returned Subscription ARN separately. |
| Direct send | `publishToEndpoint(endpointArn)` | Resolve an authorized endpoint from backend records; record acceptance for the actual operation. |
| Topic send | `publishToTopic(topicArn)` | Authorize the broadcast and inspect its configured audience before sending. |
| Unsubscribe | `unsubscribe(subscriptionArn)` | Use the stored authorized subscription, reconcile the resulting state, and update persistence. |

The SNS protocol for a mobile endpoint subscription is **`application`**. A Platform Application ARN cannot substitute for a Topic ARN, and an Endpoint ARN cannot substitute for a Subscription ARN. [Subscribe contract](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sns/latest/api/API_Subscribe.html).

For multiple topics, run separately coordinated operations and store each actual result. A failure on topic two does not roll back a successful subscription/send on topic one. Do not return one boolean that hides partial results or rerun the entire list after a timeout.

A publish message ID means **SNS acceptance**, not device display, user acknowledgement, or order success. Standard mobile push publishing does not gain exactly-once behavior from a locally generated operation ID.

## 8. Handle failures without false success

| Result | Host coordinator action |
| :--- | :--- |
| Local input/serialization rejection | Correct the input/configuration; no send should be attempted. |
| Classified SNS rejection such as authorization/invalid parameter | Preserve a sanitized category and AWS request reference where permitted; investigate the actual cause. |
| `UnknownWriteOutcome`, transport timeout, or server-side 5xx | Mark outcome unknown and reconcile existing state before another write. |
| Endpoint creation returned, database save failed | Preserve the returned association/operation evidence and reconcile persistence; do not pretend registration completed. |
| Endpoint verify read fails after an update | Readiness remains unverified; preserve the update's possible side effect. |
| Invalid/disabled provider endpoint | Obtain the current token and follow the approved reconciliation lifecycle; do not repeatedly enable a known-stale token. |

The adapter classifies transport failures and 5xx responses on its write calls conservatively. Reads can still throw SDK errors; the coordinator must retain prior step outcomes. Do not log a raw propagated SDK exception at a controller/global-handler boundary, since its message/context can contain protected identifiers. Use the approved sanitized error mapping.

