## 8. Verify without sending to real users

1. Confirm the approved package and its actual types/implementation or maintainer contract for every method used.
2. Validate `.npmrc`/CI/Docker handling without printing the credential or publishing a secret-bearing artifact.
3. Use the existing test runner with a mocked PushJS boundary to verify authorized recipient resolution, exact call arguments, and protected identifier storage.
4. Test rejection, asynchronous failure, unknown send outcome, registration persistence failure, and partial multi-topic results through the confirmed completion adapter.
5. Test token/account replacement and opt-out against the actual host contract. A stopped mobile listener does not remove a backend subscription.
6. Only through an approved non-production integration test, register one dedicated installation, send generic synthetic content, and record backend acceptance and device behavior separately.

