import { Tabs, TabItem } from '@astrojs/starlight/components';
import MermaidZoom from '../components/mermaid-zoom.astro';

A deep link asks the app to open a destination. It does not prove the sender's identity or authorize access to an order/account.

**Status:** the application's production domains, schemes, route schema, and notification link fields still require owner confirmation. This page provides a **vendor-backed integration template**, using one deliberately narrow teaching URL:

```text
https://links.example.invalid/updates
```

`example.invalid` is a placeholder. It will not verify or route as a production domain. Replace it consistently only after the domain, app identities, route, and security requirements are approved.

> **Confidential — Enterprise internal use only.** Keep private domains, signing fingerprints, association details, account data, and diagnostic evidence in approved systems. Do not put credentials, customer/order payloads, or authorization tokens in a link or log its complete raw contents.

## 1. Confirm the link contract before implementation

| Required decision | Owner-confirmed value |
| :--- | :--- |
| Domain and website owner | Actual HTTPS host, association-file hosting, and browser fallback. |
| Android identity | Final application ID and installed-app signing certificate fingerprint for each approved environment. |
| Apple identity | App identifier prefix plus bundle ID, team/capability, and matching signed entitlement. |
| Routes/parameters | Allowed destinations and exact schema, validation, and authorization behavior. |
| Startup/account policy | How to retain/discard an open before authentication or after an account switch. |
| Notification integration | Whether a payload includes a link and which existing component owns tap handling. |
| Custom schemes, if any | Exact approved scheme and collision/fallback handling; not assumed by this template. |

Prefer an owner-approved verified HTTPS App Link/Universal Link route where appropriate. Custom schemes do not establish verified website ownership and need a separate explicit decision. This template registers no custom scheme.

Do not add an `orderId`, `deepLink`, or arbitrary `url` payload property just because another app uses it. The current notification templates intentionally open a generic authorized updates destination; they do not yet define a payload-to-route contract.

## 2. Keep validation separate from authorization

| Stage | Required behavior |
| :--- | :--- |
| Receive | Capture the initial URL or later open event once through the actual app lifecycle. |
| Validate | Accept only the approved scheme/host/path and permitted parameters. Unknown or malformed input does not navigate. |
| Wait | Retain an allowed pending intent until startup, current authentication, and navigation are ready. |
| Authorize | Confirm access using current account/server state, not an identifier in the link. |
| Consume | Open the allowed destination after the host accepts it. Do not run a purchase, payment, deletion, or other business write from a link. |
| Account transition | Clear/revalidate pending intents and cancel obsolete work through the session owner. |

The sample helper uses exact equality to accept only `/updates`, with no parameters, alternative encodings, trailing slash, or fragment. It is deliberately stricter than a general URL parser. Expanding accepted syntax requires matching parser tests and a reviewed route contract.

## 3. Configure the selected platform

<Tabs>
<TabItem label="Android">

### A. Configure verified App Links

Merge into the **existing destination Activity** in `AndroidManifest.xml`; do not create multiple Activities handling the same link unintentionally:

```xml
<intent-filter android:autoVerify="true">
    <action android:name="android.intent.action.VIEW" />
    <category android:name="android.intent.category.DEFAULT" />
    <category android:name="android.intent.category.BROWSABLE" />
    <data android:scheme="https"
          android:host="links.example.invalid"
          android:path="/updates" />
</intent-filter>
```

The Activity receiving external links needs the appropriate `android:exported` configuration. Preserve existing launcher flags/task/launch-mode decisions; do not change launch mode globally merely to match a snippet. Runtime validation is still required even with an intent filter.

The website owner hosts this **template** at `https://<approved-host>/.well-known/assetlinks.json`:

