| Exact approved HTTPS `/updates` | Accepted as a generic pending destination. |
| Lookalike domain, HTTP, credentials, alternate port | Rejected. |
| Query/fragment, extra path, trailing slash, encoded variant | Rejected until explicitly added through a reviewed parser contract. |
| Valid link before authentication | No protected navigation before readiness and authorization. |
| Repeated readiness check after accepted navigation | No reconsumption without a new accepted event. |
| Account change while pending | Cleared/revalidated by the session owner; no prior-account content. |
| App absent, browser fallback, user defaults | Behavior matches the approved web/platform route; association is tested separately from parser behavior. |
| Notification tap and external URL | Each uses the single chosen event owner and authorization boundary. |

The helpers keep a single pending boolean in memory and coalesce opens. They do not persist individual links across process death, guarantee exactly-once event handling, or implement an account-specific durable queue. Extend those behaviors only against the real requirement.

